### ABOUT THIS CORPUS
The questions in this evaluation are drawn from a large multiple-choice collection spanning graduate-level subject areas across the sciences, engineering, and mathematics. Items were written and reviewed by subject-matter contributors and then filtered for ambiguity, duplication, and answer-key errors.
Every item has exactly one correct option. Options are labelled with consecutive capital letters beginning at A, and the number of options varies by item; most items have between four and ten. The position of the correct option is randomized across the corpus, so option position carries no information.
Items carry a difficulty label assigned during review. That label is not shown to you and is used only when assembling batches. Some items are primarily calculation-based and others primarily conceptual; the two kinds are interleaved rather than grouped.
